# Everything under /drugscan is published byte-for-byte.
#
# The Ascent batch files in tests/fixtures/expected are CRLF, and that is part
# of the format the instrument reads - the golden tests compare them byte for
# byte. Git's autocrlf would normalise them to LF in the index, and the Linux
# runner that builds this site would then check out LF and serve broken
# fixtures. Marking the tree as non-text disables all end-of-line conversion.
* -text
